player createDiaryRecord ["diary", ["Execution","
<font size='18'>COMMANDER'S INTENT</font>
<br/>
Our priority is the recapture of the northern camps and military installations, which hold the greatest strategic value. Camp Rogain, Mike-26, and Stratis Air Base must be back in our hands by the end of the day.
<br/>
Kamino was never stocked with hacking tools or cyber-warfare equipment, so the compromised communications towers will have to be destroyed outright to deny the enemy their use.
<br/><br/>
<font size='18'>MOVEMENT PLAN</font>
<br/>
Insertion and movement on foot or by light vehicle. Reinsertion via FOB or Rally Point.
<br/><br/>
<font size='18'>FIRE SUPPORT PLAN</font>
<br/>
UAV, artillery, CAS, and supply drops are on call.
"]];

player createDiaryRecord ["diary", ["Mission","
Regain control of Stratis. Secure all military installations, deny the enemy use of our communications infrastructure, and recover any friendly survivors.
"]];

player createDiaryRecord ["diary", ["Situation","
For the past several weeks, our unit has been conducting routine training at the Kamino Firing Range, drilling small-arms proficiency and tactical maneuvers. With no credible threats reported on Stratis, our remaining installations across the island have been held by skeleton crews. That reduced footprint, justified at the time by a low threat assessment, has left those positions dangerously exposed.
<br/>

<br/>
Earlier today, intelligence reported that multiple military sites across Stratis are under coordinated assault by local rebel forces. Initial assessments indicate the rebels are far better equipped and organized than previously believed. Surveillance shows them operating with precision, striking key sites to cripple our communications, logistics, and mobility.
<br/>

<br/>
Evidence recovered from recent skirmishes points to outside involvement. The rebels are fielding modern weapons, advanced comms gear, and tactical equipment well beyond what is normally available on the island, suggesting an off-island benefactor supplying both training and matériel to fuel the insurgency.
<br/>

<br/>
Compounding the situation, our communications towers across Stratis have been compromised in what appears to be a sophisticated hacking operation. The enemy now has partial access to our network, allowing them to monitor our movements and potentially disrupt our command structure. This breach severely limits our ability to coordinate with HQ and lends additional urgency to our response.
<br/>

<br/>
The enemy has dug into strategic positions and is exploiting their familiarity with the terrain. Their numbers remain unconfirmed but appear sufficient to sustain a prolonged occupation. Our task is to retake key locations and neutralize the rebel threat before they consolidate their hold on Stratis. Expect heavy resistance, and be prepared for reinforcements from hostile elements off-island.
<br/><br/>
<font size='18'>ENEMY FORCES</font>
<br/>
Local rebels, motorized
<br/><br/>
<font size='18'>FRIENDLY FORCES</font>
<br/>
CDF
"]];
